{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-continuity-witness","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0098","math_ordinal":207,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The primed continuity premise is for nu-prime and was introduced with E-prime and delta-prime on the preceding lines.  Using E again leaves the E-prime witness unused and does not justify the subsequent estimate.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt232.tex:235","source_normalized_sha256":"8aa17ce0c730c077f32599c4587aab1ec72a10c60b56189c3bb4bc477ea9e4f0","source_text":"$\\mu(F\\cap E)\\le\\delta'$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt232.tex:232","target_normalized_sha256":"af334d84bc6074fde7fd55e27798345ce39f4f173fbde8eeeb0c3c7f6fe684f2","target_text":"$\\mu(F\\cap E')\\le\\delta'$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S232"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-convergent-sequence","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0099","math_ordinal":334,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof defines g_n as the increasing finite suprema and then defines f as their pointwise limit.  B. Levi applies to g_n; the original f_n sequence need not be monotone or converge pointwise.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt232.tex:385","source_normalized_sha256":"73806288125df251460e83767b114b0b0af3071534cb87a08c1bc0c863c64915","source_text":"$\\int_Ef=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\int_Ef_n\\le\\nu E$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt232.tex:378","target_normalized_sha256":"353cb337bf6f4fcea1114b175e6254efaac764a5a2770acc6b48c4ce01f6b6ef","target_text":"$\\int_Ef=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\int_Eg_n\\le\\nu E$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S232"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-and-mismatched-witnesses","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0100","math_ordinal":593,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The sentence introduces separate singularity witnesses F-prime and F-double-prime.  Each must be mu-null and support its corresponding singular component; unprimed F is not introduced in this argument.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt232.tex:682-683","source_normalized_sha256":"e286197dbf648ad6e53c67aec801e51a33aac6506e9f3b1e5dbfa17a7b84f202","source_text":"$\\mu F=\\mu F'=\\nu_s'(X\\setminus F)=\\nu_s''(X\\setminus F)=0$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt232.tex:662-663","target_normalized_sha256":"96aa1e6ec2aa15e78e11842d690ff19f28f5b2d9ed2edbbdbeff16822e08cd44","target_text":"$\\mu F'=\\mu F''=\\nu_s'(X\\setminus F')=\\nu_s''(X\\setminus F'')=0$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S232"}
